    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d183-a3">

                <pb facs="0375" n="1335" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1335"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No.
                    38.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Circular of the minister of internal
                    affairs.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Internal Affairs</hi></placeName>[, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1888-10-20T23:59:59-05:00"
                            notBefore="1888-09-04T00:00:00-05:00"
                    >undated</date>].</dateline></opener>
                <p>The minister of internal affairs has addressed, under date of September 4, 1888,
                    No. 3147, section medical police, the following circular to the King’s
                    commissioners:</p>
                <p>I have the honor to inform you that I have no objection that one or two hogs
                    should be kept and fed on board of sea-going vessels, provided they are not to
                    be unloaded, but killed on board, or exported again with the same vessel, or to
                    the use of fresh, dried, and salted hog meat and pork as provision on board,
                    without, however, exempting them from the prohibition in the King’s resolution
                    of August 14, 1888 (Staatsblad No. 142), as to free import.</p>
                <p>The inspectors of taxes in the different provinces are hereby notified of this
                    regulation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mackay</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >The Minister of Internal Affairs.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
